INT. GOAT YOGA STUDIO - MORNING

A converted barn. Bamboo mats in neat rows, string lights, a chalkboard reading "Namaste Baa-ck." Six goats wander the floor, bored, chewing yoga straps.

CLAUDETTE FONTENOT, 40s, instructor, flowing linen, sits cross-legged on a mat with a phone propped against her water bottle. LEONARD PRICE, 50s, her only student, a stockbroker in too-tight spandex, attempts a downward dog.

LEONARD
Claudette, one of them is eating my sock.

CLAUDETTE
That's Beyonce. She loves attention.

LEONARD
It's attention with teeth.

CLAUDETTE
Breathe, Leonard. In through the nose.

He breathes. Beyonce chews. He breathes again.

The phone rings. A photo of an elderly woman in a floppy hat. MAMA ROSE.

CLAUDETTE (CONT'D)
Sorry. I have to take this.

She answers on speaker.

MAMA ROSE (V.O.)
Claudette! Are you on the goat farm again?

CLAUDETTE
It's a studio, Mama.

MAMA ROSE (V.O.)
Is it the goat that eats the shoes?

LEONARD
(under his breath)
That's the one.

MAMA ROSE (V.O.)
Who's that? A man? Are you seeing a man?

CLAUDETTE
It's a client, Mama.

MAMA ROSE (V.O.)
He sounds fat.

LEONARD
I'm in a very difficult pose.

MAMA ROSE (V.O.)
Claudette, I need you to come home. The faucet is leaking again.

CLAUDETTE
I'll call a plumber.

MAMA ROSE (V.O.)
Plumbers are thieves.

CLAUDETTE
Mama, I love you. I have to teach.

MAMA ROSE (V.O.)
Is the goat singing? I hear a goat singing.

On cue, Beyonce bleats, triumphant.

CLAUDETTE
(to Leonard)
She's proud of you.

LEONARD
I'll be sure to thank her.

CLAUDETTE
Goodbye, Mama.

She hangs up. Smooths her linen. Resettles.

CLAUDETTE (CONT'D)
Where were we?

LEONARD
Paying for this.

CLAUDETTE
Right. Warrior One.
